      "api_error_status": null,
      "result": "I implemented `diagnose` and `cost_summary` in `operations.py` and wrote up the results in `DOSSIER.md`. The supplied suite (`python -m unittest discover -s tests`) failed with 17 errors on the stubs and passes (13 tests, OK) after the change. I did not run protected acceptance, which the operator invokes separately.\n\n**Contract.** `docs/contract.md`, `docs/G4-OD-01.md` and `docs/G4-SCHEMA-MAP.json` don't conflict. The `booking.py` SHA-256 matches the one the owner recorded, so I did not need to stop and ask.\n\n**Acceptance example.** A `booking.init_db` database (table `reservations_v3`) with one active row plus an inserted overlapping active row gives `ACTIVE_OVERLAP` with pairs `[[1,2]]` and unchanged file bytes. A cancelled row does not trigger it. `reservations_v3` with other columns, or next to `reservations`, raises `ValueError`.\n\n**Changes in `operations.py`**\n- **`diagnose`:**\n  - It opens the file read-only, never creates it, and requires schema version 3.\n  - It matches the full column signature of the three named layouts plus the mapped `reservations_v3` from `docs/G4-SCHEMA-MAP.json`. Zero or more than one match raises `ValueError`.\n  - It compares file digests before and after, and raises `RuntimeError` if they differ.\n- **`cost_summary`:** it sums every attempt with `Decimal`. Non-numeric, `None`, bool, NaN, infinite and negative values raise `ValueError`. Zero accepted outcomes returns null unit metrics and `NO_ACCEPTED_OUTCOME`.\n\n**Other checks.** An extra probe confirmed a wrong-signature table is refused, `reservations` plus mapped `reservations_v3` is refused as competing, and a fresh database diagnoses cleanly.\n\n**Remaining uncertainty**\n- No concurrent-writer test was run. The digest check would miss a change that is reverted between the two reads, and it does not hash WAL sidecar files.\n- `\"1e999\"` is accepted as a finite number. The contract doesn't address it, so I added no rule.\n- \"The three proposals\" in the dossier's Decide section aren't defined in the supplied files, so I made no per-proposal call. I recorded ACCEPT, REJECT and ASK for the increment as a whole instead.\n- I observed no human approval.\n\nOnly `operations.py` and `DOSSIER.md` were edited. The probe script is in the scratchpad, outside the project.",
